TTYCHATTER.MAILBOT(1)       User Commands       TTYCHATTER.MAILBOT(1)

NAME
    ttychatter.mailbot - IMAP/sendmail or SMTP transport adapter and remote
    control surface for ttychatter

SYNOPSIS
    ttychatter.mailbot --once [--dry-run]
    ttychatter.mailbot --daemon [--dry-run]
    ttychatter.mailbot --list-candidates
    ttychatter.mailbot --doctor
    ttychatter.mailbot --sessions
    ttychatter.mailbot --list-sessions
    ttychatter.mailbot --manpage
    ttychatter.mailbot --update-models [--dry-run]
    ttychatter.mailbot --config
    ttychatter.mailbot --set KEY VALUE
    ttychatter.mailbot --unset KEY
    ttychatter.mailbot --set-imap-password [--gpg]
    ttychatter.mailbot --set-smtp-password [--gpg]
    ttychatter.mailbot --version
    ttychatter.mailbot --help

DESCRIPTION
    ttychatter.mailbot reads unread mail from an IMAP mailbox, selects messages
    whose subject contains a token such as tc:{session}, and either:

        1. sends the message body and attachments to ttychatter.python; or
        2. handles an allowlisted mailbot control command.

    Replies are sent by sendmail or SMTP. The mailbot does not implement
    OpenRouter, model selection, memory, or session context itself. It remains a
    transport adapter:

        email -> ttychatter.python -> email reply

    Ordinary chat runs use ttychatter.python --loopback so stdout is the clean
    response body and stderr remains diagnostic output. Utility/control commands
    call ttychatter.python directly with explicit allowlisted flags.

SUBJECT FORMAT
    Normal chat request:

        tc:{session-name}

    New timestamped session:

        tc:{new}

    Mailbot config export/update:

        tc:{CONFIG}

    Mailbot control command in the subject:

        tc:{MAILBOT:command args}

    Mailbot control command in the body:

        tc:{MAILBOT}

        command args

    The subject token can appear inside a larger subject line. The prefix tc,
    the CONFIG token, and the MAILBOT token are configurable.

EMAIL CONTROL COMMANDS
    All control commands require the message sender to match ALLOWED_FROM.

    help
        Return the mailbot email command summary.

    manpage
    manual
    get-manpage
    fetch-manpage
        Return the configured external manpage as an attachment named
        ttychatter.mailbot.1 when found, otherwise return the embedded fallback.
        This is the command to fetch and retrieve the mailbot manpage over email.

    config
        Return the public/redacted mailbot config as an attachment named
        ttychatter-mailbot-config.txt. This is equivalent to the tc:{CONFIG}
        export path.

    sessions
    list
    list-sessions
    session-list
        List saved session logs newest first. Each entry includes the sanitized
        session name, modified time, byte count, line count, and short previews
        from the head and tail of the log.

    search TEXT
        Search all session logs for TEXT, newest first.

    search-session SESSION TEXT
        Search one session log for TEXT.

    rename-session OLD NEW
        Rename one session log. Names are sanitized to A-Z, a-z, 0-9, dot,
        underscore, and dash. Dry-run reports the action without renaming.

    update-models
    update-model-list
    update-model-cache
    model-cache
        Run ttychatter.python --update-models. The mailbot then looks for a
        cache path printed as "updated model cache: PATH"; if no path is found,
        it uses MODEL_CACHE_FILE. When the cache exists and is not larger than
        MAX_OUTGOING_ATTACHMENT_BYTES, the reply attaches it as models-cache.json.

    models [FLAGS]
        Run ttychatter.python --models with safe model-list flags only.

    routers [FLAGS]
    router-list [FLAGS]
        Run ttychatter.python --routers with safe model-list flags only.

    Allowed model-list flags are:

        --all
        --sort VALUE
        --modellist-sort-tokens
        --min-input-tokens N
        --min-output-tokens N
        --hide-preview
        --show-preview
        --require-tokens
        --allow-missing-tokens
        --model-type VALUE

    favorites
    faves
        Run ttychatter.python --favorites.

    favorite-model MODEL
        Run ttychatter.python --favorite-model MODEL.

    unfavorite-model MODEL
    unbookmark-model MODEL
        Run ttychatter.python --unfavorite-model MODEL.

    test-model MODEL
        Run ttychatter.python --test-model MODEL.

    ttyconfig
    ttyconfig-summary
        Run ttychatter.python --config.

    ttydoctor
    doctor
        Run ttychatter.python --doctor.

    credits
        Run ttychatter.python --credits.

    show-memory SESSION
        Run ttychatter.python --show-memory SESSION.

    clear-memory SESSION
        Run ttychatter.python --clear-memory SESSION.

    tty-set KEY VALUE
        Run ttychatter.python --set KEY VALUE. The mailbot refuses to set
        OPENROUTER_API_KEY or API_KEY by email. Use ttychatter.python
        --set-api-key locally for secrets.

    tty-unset KEY
        Run ttychatter.python --unset KEY.

BODY ARGUMENTS
    For commands that usually need arguments, the subject may contain only the
    command name and the first nonempty nonquoted body line may contain the
    arguments. This works for models, routers, search, search-session,
    rename-session, favorite-model, unfavorite-model, test-model, show-memory,
    clear-memory, tty-set, and tty-unset.

    Example:

        Subject: tc:{MAILBOT:search}

        gpt-5

LOCAL COMMANDS
    --config-file PATH
        Use an alternate mailbot config file. This option applies before local
        commands such as --manpage, --sessions, --update-models, and --config.

    --once
        Check unread messages once and exit.

    --daemon
        Poll forever using POLL_INTERVAL.

    --dry-run
        Show replies/actions without sending replies, replacing config,
        recording processed Message-IDs, mutating model caches, renaming
        sessions, or marking messages seen.

    --list-candidates
        Print unread From/Subject/Message-ID values and whether each message
        matches or why it is skipped. Uses IMAP BODY.PEEK[] and does not mark
        messages read.

    --doctor
        Print local diagnostics for config, directories, password files, manpage
        lookup, send method, and ttychatter command setting.

    --sessions, --list-sessions
        Print the same session list and head/tail previews used by the email
        sessions command.

    --manpage
        Print the configured external manpage to stdout when found, otherwise
        print the embedded fallback.

    --update-models
        Run the email update-models dispatcher locally. It prints the subprocess
        result and cache attachment note to stdout. The local CLI does not send
        an email attachment.

    --config
        Print nonsecret config diagnostics.

    --set KEY VALUE, --unset KEY
        Edit the mailbot config file.

    --set-imap-password [--gpg]
    --set-smtp-password [--gpg]
        Prompt for IMAP or SMTP password storage. With --gpg, store the secret
        encrypted by external gpg. Without --gpg, store it in plaintext config.

CONFIGURATION BY EMAIL
    A message from ALLOWED_FROM with subject tc:{CONFIG} and no config
    attachment causes the bot to reply with the current public config as
    ttychatter-mailbot-config.txt. Plaintext IMAP_PASSWORD and SMTP_PASSWORD
    values are redacted.

    To update config by email:

        1. Send tc:{CONFIG}.
        2. Save and edit the attached config file.
        3. Reply with the edited text config attached under the same subject.
        4. Run ttychatter.mailbot --once, or let daemon/cron process it.

    The bot creates a timestamped backup before replacing the config. Dry-run
    reports what would happen but does not write config.

