MANPAGE LOOKUP
    The email manpage command and local --manpage option return the first
    readable manpage found. The lookup order is:

        TTYCHATTER_MAILBOT_MANPAGE_FILE from environment, when set
        MAILBOT_MANPAGE_FILE from config
        ~/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/ttychatter.mailbot.1
        ~/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/ttychatter.mailbot.1.gz
        directory beside the script/ttychatter.mailbot.1
        directory beside the script/ttychatter.mailbot.1.gz
        directory beside argv[0]/ttychatter.mailbot.1
        directory beside argv[0]/ttychatter.mailbot.1.gz
        $XDG_DATA_HOME/man/man1/ttychatter.mailbot.1
        $XDG_DATA_HOME/man/man1/ttychatter.mailbot.1.gz
        ~/.local/share/man/man1/ttychatter.mailbot.1
        ~/.local/share/man/man1/ttychatter.mailbot.1.gz
        /usr/local/share/man/man1/ttychatter.mailbot.1
        /usr/local/share/man/man1/ttychatter.mailbot.1.gz
        /usr/local/man/man1/ttychatter.mailbot.1
        /usr/local/man/man1/ttychatter.mailbot.1.gz
        /usr/share/man/man1/ttychatter.mailbot.1
        /usr/share/man/man1/ttychatter.mailbot.1.gz
        current working directory/ttychatter.mailbot.1
        current working directory/ttychatter.mailbot.1.gz

    For a normal install, name the file ttychatter.mailbot.1 rather than
    ttychatter.mailbot.1.updated. To use a different filename, set
    MAILBOT_MANPAGE_FILE. If no external file is found, the embedded fallback
    is used.

IMAP SAFETY
    The mailbot inspects unread candidates using IMAP BODY.PEEK[]. Ordinary
    RFC822/BODY fetches may set the \Seen flag. Dry-run, candidate listing,
    skipped messages, config inspection, and command inspection are designed not
    to consume unread state. A matching message is marked seen only after a
    successful real processing run, and only if MARK_SEEN is enabled.

ALLOWLIST BEHAVIOR
    ALLOWED_FROM is the main safety gate. It may contain one address or multiple
    addresses separated by commas, semicolons, or whitespace. Matching is
    case-insensitive after parsing the From header to a bare address.

    A wildcard value of * is accepted for temporary local testing but should not
    be left in production.

SECURITY NOTES
    Use a narrow ALLOWED_FROM and a private mailbox. Commands are allowlisted and
    are not shell-expanded. TTYCHATTER_EXTRA_ARGS is used for ordinary loopback
    chat calls, not for utility/control calls. Do not send passwords, API keys,
    or other long-lived secrets through email.

FILES
    ~/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/config
    ~/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/imap-password.gpg
    ~/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/smtp-password.gpg
    ~/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/ttychatter.mailbot.1
    ~/.local/share/man/man1/ttychatter.mailbot.1
    /usr/local/share/man/man1/ttychatter.mailbot.1
    ~/.local/state/ttychatter/mailbot/processed-ids.txt
    ~/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/sessions/*.log
    ~/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/models-cache.json

EXIT STATUS
    0 indicates success. Nonzero status indicates configuration, IMAP, SMTP,
    sendmail, or ttychatter subprocess failure.

